Chapter 16
Net present value and the internal rate of return
القيمة الحالية الصافية ومعدل العائد الداخلي
Chapter 14 built the cash flows and Chapter 15 chose the rate. This chapter puts them together in the two measures that decide most capital investments: net present value, which states the value a project creates in money, and the internal rate of return, which states it as a rate.
They usually agree. Where they disagree, net present value is right and the reasons it is right are themselves examinable. This chapter computes both for the roasting line, sets out what each assumes, works through the three situations in which they part company, and ends with the modified internal rate of return, which repairs the worst of the problems.
Figure F716-01 is your map.
Figure F716-01. Chapter 16 roadmap: the two measures, what they assume, and where they disagree.
