LANGUAGE FOCUS   "Internal" and "net"
Two adjectives in this chapter's titles do real work. Internal in internal rate of return means computed from the project's own flows, with no external rate used — which is both its appeal and the source of every one of its faults, because a measure that needs no cost of capital also ignores one. Arabic معدل العائد الداخلي and French taux de rendement interne both translate internal literally, so the word travels. Net in net present value means after deducting the investment: the present value of what comes in, less the present value of what goes out. Candidates who compute 4,441,630 and stop have found a present value and not a net present value, and the missing word costs the mark. Arabic صافية and French nette carry exactly the same instruction: subtract what you put in.
